<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">István Bethlen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1874">1874</a>–<a href="/years/1946">1946</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Count István Bethlen was prime minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> from 1921 to 1931. A Transylvanian aristocrat, he stabilised the post-war kingdom under Regent Horthy, restored open voting in the countryside, obtained a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-nations">League of Nations</a> loan and sought allies, notably <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, for revising the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-trianon">Treaty of Trianon</a>. Arrested by Soviet forces in 1945, he died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/istvan-bethlen.jpg" alt="István Bethlen" width="320" height="382" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bethlen_Istv%C3%A1n_1930s.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
